    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** providing the clear anchor for the lineup; his score of 82.97 is fueled by a elite xwOBA of 0.477 and a favorable matchup against Fedde, where the SP skill projection offers a massive 19% boost. Alongside him, **Trea Turner** and **Colt Keith** occupy high-leverage leadoff spots, both benefiting from substantial lineup positioning adjustments. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** remains a primary target for our stolen base strategy, as his 14% platoon edge against Ashcraft keeps his efficiency well above the 60-threshold despite a difficult matchup against an elite arm. We are also leaning heavily into the platoon advantages for **Casey Schmitt**, whose score of 54.09 is buoyed by an 11% platoon boost and favorable wind conditions out, making him a viable play despite facing a pitcher who effectively controls the run game.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Josh Smith**, who fell just short of our 40-point \"Zebras Floor\" with a 38.43 score. While his platoon advantage against Gilbert was appealing, the combination of a difficult SP matchup (-16% skill adjustment) and poor historical BvP data over 26 plate appearances ultimately rendered him a liability compared to the higher-floor options we started. Looking at the lineup, we are monitoring the status of **Trea Turner** and **Kyle Schwarber** closely; both are currently listed as \"Lineup Pending.\" While we have modeled them assuming their standard #1 and #2 spots, any shift in the batting order against Warren could necessitate a rapid re-evaluation of their respective projections. **Christian Yelich** and **Hyeseong Kim** remain sidelined, leaving us to navigate a narrow path through today's SP matchups while protecting our daily game caps.",
